    "['unit [unit_number] family [family_type] vlan members [vlan_id]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated HUAWEI equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0\\n port link-type access\\n port default vlan 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In HUAWEI devices, we create a subinterface (GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0) similar to Juniper's unit 0\\n- We set the port as access mode (equivalent to ethernet-switching)\\n- We assign VLAN 10 as the default VLAN (equivalent to vlan members 10)\\n- The command structure is different but achieves the same result of assigning VLAN 10 to the interface in access mode\", 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'port link-type access', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated HUAWEI equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0\\n port link-type access\\n port default vlan 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In HUAWEI devices, we create a subinterface (GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0) similar to Juniper's unit 0\\n- We set the port as access mode (equivalent to ethernet-switching)\\n- We assign VLAN 10 as the default VLAN (equivalent to vlan members 10)\\n- The command structure is different but achieves the same result of assigning VLAN 10 to the interface in access mode\", 'trans_template': 'port link-type access'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'port default vlan 10', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated HUAWEI equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0\\n port link-type access\\n port default vlan 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In HUAWEI devices, we create a subinterface (GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0) similar to Juniper's unit 0\\n- We set the port as access mode (equivalent to ethernet-switching)\\n- We assign VLAN 10 as the default VLAN (equivalent to vlan members 10)\\n- The command structure is different but achieves the same result of assigning VLAN 10 to the interface in access mode\", 'trans_template': 'port default vlan 10'}]]": 1,
    "['unit [parameter2] encapsulation vlan-ccc', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'vlan-type dot1q 10', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent HUAWEI command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nvlan-type dot1q 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper's `encapsulation vlan-ccc` with `vlan-id 10` creates a VLAN CCC subinterface for VLAN 10\\n- In HUAWEI, we use `vlan-type dot1q` to specify the VLAN encapsulation on a subinterface\\n- The VLAN ID (10 in this case) is specified directly in the command\\n- Note that HUAWEI doesn't have an exact equivalent of Juniper's CCC (Circuit Cross Connect) family, so additional MPLS/transport configuration might be needed depending on the full context\", 'trans_template': 'vlan-type dot1q 10'}]]": 1,
